    cases: [
      { id: "qna-case-covshift-diagnosis-01", level: 3, q: "Your LinUCB-served recommendations have quietly gotten worse for a growing segment of users who joined the platform recently, even though nothing about the model code changed. Walk through how you'd figure out whether this is a covariate-shift issue and what you'd check first.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-alpha-regression-01", level: 3, q: "A LinUCB deployment that was performing well starts showing a drop in realized reward relative to what its design would predict, and you suspect the exploration parameter is miscalibrated. Walk through your diagnostic process and how you'd decide whether to change it.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-hybrid-migration-01", level: 3, q: "A teammate wants to migrate a disjoint LinUCB deployment to the hybrid model because they've noticed arms seem to respond similarly to certain user features. Walk through how you'd evaluate whether that migration is actually worth the added complexity.", difficulty: "hard" },
      { id: "qna-case-latency-scale-01", level: 3, q: "Your LinUCB service's per-request latency has been creeping up as you've added more contextual features and arms. Walk through how you'd figure out whether the online update step is the bottleneck, and what you'd change if it is.", difficulty: "hard" },
      { id: "qna-case-coldstart-bug-01", level: 3, q: "A newly added arm with zero prior observations is getting almost no traffic, which shouldn't happen given how LinUCB is designed to treat unobserved arms. Walk through what you'd expect to happen instead, and where you'd look for the actual bug.", difficulty: "medium" }
    ],
