      { id: "qna-case-low-neff-01", level: 3, q: "Your OPE pipeline reports plenty of logged data overall, but effective sample size for one specific candidate policy is very low. Walk me through what's actually happening and what you'd do about it before trusting that policy's estimate.", difficulty: "hard" },
      { id: "qna-case-propensity-bug-01", level: 3, q: "After shipping a change, someone discovers that propensities were being reconstructed from an old snapshot of the logging policy instead of logged live at serve time. Walk me through how you'd expect this to show up in your OPE numbers, and how you'd fix the logging process going forward.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-estimator-choice-01", level: 3, q: "You need to rank dozens of candidate policies that diverge substantially from the current production policy before picking a few for online testing. Walk me through which estimator(s) you'd reach for and why, given what you know about how each one behaves under large policy divergence.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-adaptive-logger-01", level: 3, q: "You learn that the logging policy generating your training data was itself a bandit that kept adapting online while it ran. Walk me through why this complicates your OPE approach and what you'd change about how you evaluate a new policy against these logs.", difficulty: "hard" }
